      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Headache management requires a comprehensive strategy that includes accurate diagnosis, reassurance and education of the patient, nonpharmacologic methods of preventing attacks, and appropriate use of prophylactic and abortive medications. Personal input from the physician and judicious selection of headache medications are crucial. Implementation of such a strategy gives patients greater ability to control and cope with their headaches."},
